 "findings": [
  "The canonical CauseWay master logo (10,018,081-byte PNG, shown at 138-140 CSS px) is about 96-99% of every cold page. It is never redrawn, regenerated, recoloured or cropped here; web-size derivatives approved by the owner are release-only engineering (TOOL-02). This is the one change that dominates the footprint.",
  "Without the logo a cold page transfers roughly 0.09-0.45 MB in four requests (HTML, one stylesheet, one script); the modelled gzip transfer is a fraction of that.",
  "Search loads a 1.97 MB local index on first use (about 0.32 MB with gzip); it is fetched only when Search is opened.",
  "Nothing is loaded from a third party: no web font, analytics, tracker or CDN (gate F6-G05)."
 ],
 "uncertainty": "Single run per page on one machine; byte counts are exact for this build and server, request timing is not measured. Real transfer depends on compression, protocol overheads, caching headers and the final design; the modelled gzip figure is an estimate. No figure here may be presented as the operational or carbon footprint of the released site.",
